WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.509 --> 00:00:17.017
The next time Pollyanna visited Mrs.

2
00:00:17.077 --> 00:00:19.978
Snow, the woman was lying in bed with the curtains closed.

3
00:00:19.998 --> 00:00:24.101
"I wish you'd come yesterday," Mrs.

4
00:00:24.141 --> 00:00:25.902
Snow said in an irritable voice.

5
00:00:25.922 --> 00:00:28.984
"I wanted you yesterday."

6
00:00:30.772 --> 00:00:34.714
"Then I'm glad I'm only a day late," Pollyanna said cheerfully.

7
00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:38.015
"It's awfully dark in here."

8
00:00:39.976 --> 00:00:42.157
Pollyanna crossed the room and opened the curtains.

9
00:00:42.177 --> 00:00:46.118
"I brought you a surprise and left it with Milly in the kitchen.

10
00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:52.081
I'll give you a hint—think of something you'd like."

11
00:00:54.342 --> 00:00:55.482
Mrs. Snow frowned.

12
00:00:56.623 --> 00:01:01.617
She was used to saying what she didn't want; she had no idea what she did want.

13
00:01:03.077 --> 00:01:03.857
"Chicken soup?"

14
00:01:05.478 --> 00:01:07.238
"I've got that," Pollyanna said.

15
00:01:07.258 --> 00:01:10.759
"No, I've changed my mind.

16
00:01:11.099 --> 00:01:12.060
Lamb stew."

17
00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:16.381
"I've got that and beef stew too!

18
00:01:17.461 --> 00:01:20.342
Nancy and I made them all, so you'd have something you like."

19
00:01:21.902 --> 00:01:23.783
Mrs. Snow didn't know how to respond.

20
00:01:24.663 --> 00:01:27.904
But that wasn't a problem because Pollyanna went right on talking.

21
00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:32.502
"I've played the game and found something for you to be glad about.

22
00:01:33.723 --> 00:01:36.385
It was extra hard because you have to stay in bed.

23
00:01:37.346 --> 00:01:39.847
But the game is even more fun when it's hard."

24
00:01:39.867 --> 00:01:42.509
"What game?"

25
00:01:43.550 --> 00:01:44.711
Mrs. Snow was puzzled.

26
00:01:44.731 --> 00:01:49.654
"Wait!" Pollyanna took a deep breath.

27
00:01:50.995 --> 00:01:54.798
"You can be glad that other people aren't as sick as you are!"

28
00:01:54.818 --> 00:01:57.880
"Well, really!"

29
00:01:58.848 --> 00:02:02.491
Mrs. Snow was angry now, but Pollyanna was happily unaware of that.

30
00:02:02.511 --> 00:02:05.334
"I'll tell you about the Glad Game."

31
00:02:05.694 --> 00:02:09.377
Pollyanna told the story of wanting a doll but receiving crutches instead.

32
00:02:10.939 --> 00:02:14.842
Just then Milly came in to announce that Miss Polly wanted Pollyanna to hurry home.

33
00:02:16.083 --> 00:02:16.724
"All right."

34
00:02:17.885 --> 00:02:18.866
Pollyanna sighed.

35
00:02:18.886 --> 00:02:20.507
"I'll hurry."

36
00:02:21.748 --> 00:02:22.569
Suddenly she laughed.

37
00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:25.631
"I guess I'm glad I have legs to hurry with!"

38
00:02:28.576 --> 00:02:32.800
Mrs. Snow didn't respond, but Milly noticed there were tears on her mother's cheeks.

39
00:02:37.103 --> 00:02:41.747
Although it was raining the next time Pollyanna saw the man, she greeted him with a bright smile.

40
00:02:43.109 --> 00:02:45.070
He didn't even bother to grunt in response.

41
00:02:47.052 --> 00:02:51.035
Pollyanna assumed he had trouble hearing, so she spoke more loudly the next day.

42
00:02:51.055 --> 00:02:56.000
"I'm glad the sun is shining today, aren't you?"

43
00:02:57.516 --> 00:02:59.878
Pollyanna bent down to pat the dog with the man.

44
00:03:00.939 --> 00:03:02.140
The man scowled at her.

45
00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:06.123
"I've got other things to think about besides the weather.

46
00:03:07.304 --> 00:03:09.506
I don't know whether the sun is shining or not."

47
00:03:11.507 --> 00:03:12.808
Pollyanna smiled brightly.

48
00:03:12.828 --> 00:03:17.432
"That's exactly why I mentioned the sun—so you'd notice it!

49
00:03:18.553 --> 00:03:21.635
I knew you'd be glad about the sunshine if you stopped to think about it."

50
00:03:23.577 --> 00:03:27.080
The man started to walk away but abruptly turned around to face her again.

51
00:03:28.192 --> 00:03:30.953
"Why don't you find someone your own age to talk to?"

52
00:03:30.973 --> 00:03:36.434
"I'd like to, sir, but there's nobody my age around right now.

53
00:03:37.395 --> 00:03:38.435
And I like old folks.

54
00:03:39.415 --> 00:03:43.536
You see, I'm used to the Ladies' Aid—" "The Ladies' Aid?

55
00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:45.177
Is that what you thought I was?"

56
00:03:46.957 --> 00:03:48.498
The man was trying not to smile.

57
00:03:50.218 --> 00:03:51.759
Pollyanna laughed gleefully.

58
00:03:51.779 --> 00:03:54.279
"Oh no, sir!

59
00:03:54.659 --> 00:03:56.440
You don't look at all like a Ladies' Aider.

60
00:03:57.576 --> 00:04:01.857
In fact, I'm sure you're much nicer than you look."

61
00:04:01.877 --> 00:04:05.998
"What?" The man strode away.

62
00:04:08.179 --> 00:04:11.860
But the next time they met, the man spoke to Pollyanna before she could greet him.

63
00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:13.900
"Good afternoon!

64
00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:17.541
Perhaps I should say right away that I know the sun's shining."

65
00:04:19.122 --> 00:04:21.682
"I knew you knew it as soon as I saw you.

66
00:04:22.983 --> 00:04:25.583
I could see it in your eyes and your smile."

67
00:04:27.692 --> 00:04:28.692
"Humph!" grunted the man.

68
00:04:30.293 --> 00:04:32.773
But he continued to talk to Pollyanna whenever they met.

69
00:04:34.834 --> 00:04:37.975
One day Nancy happened to be with Pollyanna when the man greeted her.

70
00:04:41.876 --> 00:04:43.456
that man just speak to you?"

71
00:04:44.637 --> 00:04:46.657
Nancy's eyes were wide with amazement.

72
00:04:46.677 --> 00:04:50.418
"He hasn't spoken to anyone for years."

73
00:04:50.438 --> 00:04:54.719
"He speaks to me, but he's never told me his name."

74
00:04:54.739 --> 00:05:00.821
"That's John Pendleton, and he lives by himself in a mansion on Pendleton Hill.

75
00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:06.422
Few people have ever seen inside his house because he doesn't like visitors.

76
00:05:07.683 --> 00:05:10.824
He's the richest man in town but doesn't like to spend his money."

77
00:05:10.844 --> 00:05:16.385
"Maybe he's saving it for orphans overseas or something," Pollyanna said.

78
00:05:16.405 --> 00:05:18.345
"I doubt it."

79
00:05:18.606 --> 00:05:19.326
Nancy went on.

80
00:05:19.346 --> 00:05:21.786
"Everybody thinks he's mysterious.

81
00:05:23.587 --> 00:05:28.821
Some years he spends most of his time traveling to faraway places like Egypt."

82
00:05:30.242 --> 00:05:32.124
"He's different," Pollyanna said.

83
00:05:32.144 --> 00:05:35.126
"But a different kind of different than Mrs.

84
00:05:35.206 --> 00:05:39.570
Snow. I'm gladder than ever that he speaks to me now!"
